+### Warehouse source column references
+
+When exporting a direct SQL column reference for a `warehouse-table` source,
+`ossie-to-sigma` writes `[physical_table/column]` instead of `[column]`. The latter
+can refer to the output column itself in Sigma. The table prefix comes from the
+emitted source path, not the Ossie dataset name; renaming the dataset or the output
+field therefore does not change which physical column is read.
+
+This qualification applies only to direct column expressions, including parenthesized
+references and references qualified by the current dataset name. It does not rewrite
+calculated expressions, element-scoped metrics, native `SIGMA` formulas, or formulas
+for `sql`, `table`, `data-model`, `join`, and `union` sources. Native overrides keep
+their existing precedence. Fully qualified SQL paths and source-path parsing are
+outside this change.
+
+See Sigma's [warehouse and calculated column representation example](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/example-representation-data-model-with-a-table-and-a-calculated-column).
+Offline conversion tests do not substitute for querying the resulting model in Sigma.
+
 ### Relationship resolution
 
 Sigma relationships (`element.relationships[]`) join two *elements*, not two *Ossie datasets*
